{
 "item": "26",
 "title": "Dipole-wall collision: the checks of micro-inertia, saturation and resolution",
 "status": "final",
 "caption": "Three checks of the dipole-wall collision of table 22 (Re = 625 on nu_inf, K = 3, w = 0 on every wall), with the definitions and the noise floor of table 22 (relative changes, absolute ones for times and distances in W / U and W). (1) The micro-inertia: l = W / 50 with j = l^2 / 100 (the relaxation time rho j / (2 kappa) of w 0.001 W / U instead of 0.10), against the control and against the run with j = l^2. (2) The saturation: l = W / 25 (40 dx), j = l^2 / 100, Lambda / l = 0.13; the strength of its primary core before the collision (t = 0.25) shows the bulk effect on the cores (r0 = 2.5 l). (3) The resolution of l: l = W / 50 at W / dx = 500 (l = 10 dx) against the control at the same resolution, beside the same l at 20 dx (the reference column, the run of table 22). The kinetic energy and the enstrophy at t = 0.25 show the effect in the bulk before the collision. The primary core is tracked as the strongest extremum within reach in every column (the reference too: its core rows can differ from table 22, which follows the nearest one); its vorticity maximum moves by 2.3 % at half the Mach number, a bias common to runs of the same Mach number. All runs on the solver trees of thesis-ch5-rc2, the same dt per resolution (the acoustic step; the angular-diffusion limit of j = l^2 / 100 is 3.5e-6 W / U, above the step 1.25e-6).",
 "files": [
